 low carbon  technology these fields and then for  environment again Sciences as a diploma  also law and economics are welcome to  apply and the experience could be in for  instance a sustainable economy in  biodiversity in ecosystem protection for  instance  then there's also a language Criterium  you always need two EU languages one of  which must be English and one of those  languages should be at least at level C1  and the other at least at level B2  the selection procedure follows the  normal path so to say so everything  starts with an application online  the first stage is what we call a talent  screener I will explain in a minute and  then the second stage is an assessment  center where candidates sit a number of  tests  successful candidates will then be  recruited mainly by the commission this  time in the director generals dealing  with energy climate and environments  so the first stage is of course or the  first step to take is the application  therefore you need an epsil account if  you already have one you use that one  you do not create a new account if you  do not have one yet you can easily  create one on our website  then you have to apply of course you'll  find the link to apply on the home page  of our website  and you can fill your application in any  of the 24 official EU languages  the talent screener part must be filled  in English  and the talent screener is a set of  questions to assess your qualifications  and experience I'll come back to that in  a minute and only that part must be  filled out in English  you have to validate your application  the latest on the 22nd of November noon  Brussels time so until then during the  whole application period you can go in  and out of your application and save  your entries but you have to validate by  the closing date  everybody who applies will then go  through this Talent screening stage so  you don't have to do anything more at  this stage you have filled out this part  basically this is a set of between six  and eight questions depending on the  field you have chosen  via which the selection board will  assess your qualifications and  experience in the field and the best  ranked will then go through to the next  stage which is an assessment center and  in this assessment center we will test a  set of skills and competencies  the first test to take is a test where  we assess your reasoning skills we test  your verbal numerical and abstract  reasoning skills  and you should take this test in the  other language than English so not  English but your other chosen language  you see the number of questions  mentioned here also the duration of the  tests  the marking overall you should  obtain at least 20 out of 40 combined  for these three reason skills tests  at the bottom of this slide you see a  link to our website where you can find  sample tests so I really advise you  to prepare this to train this  in this way you get to know the level of  difficulty of these questions  and also important you must be able that  you you should be able to solve these  questions under time pressure because  there is a Time factor involved in these  tests and by training this through our  website for instance you get you know to  know how this works and how good you are  and if need be you can prepare more and  rehearse this a bit  we have sample tests available in all  languages so you can really pick your  language and train this  the second test to take will assess a  set of General competencies we have  eight competencies to be tested and we  do this through two tests you will sit a  case study which is a written exercise  and through this case study we will test  four competence if you see them here  and then you will also sit an interview  which is a situational Competency Based  interview basically meaning that we put  you in a work related situation and we  want to see how you react  given the given the situation  through this interview we will test the  four other competencies  you will see this test in English Okay  you see the mark you mentioned and the  pass Mark again you need a combined pass  Mark of 40 out of 80.  after having tested the general  competencies of course we also test the  field related competencies your  knowledge in the field of the  competition and we do this through an  interview  marked on 100 points of course quite  important quite clearly and you need at  least 50 out of 100 to pass  the best ranked candidates will end up  on the list of successful candidates you  see again the number of people we're  looking for here and these are the  people that then will be recruited by  these different services in the  commission uh in the months to come  after publication of this list  this is what I wanted to share with you  if you want to have the full detail you  should of course read the notice of  competition which is this big legal  document giving you all the information  on the job description on what you need  to know and do on the different stages  of the competition uh gives you all the  information very detently so please do  read it if you do have more questions  for us you can reach out to us through  the website  we have a contact form available there  and you can reach out to us and we can  we will reply to each question you have  about this competition  you can also follow us on social media  to stay updated on upcoming  opportunities  for now I wish you all the luck with the  application and the testing in this  competition and maybe you will join us  someday in the future in the EU  institutions bye-bye
 

